 any extra comments or explanations, just the YAML tasks. Each task should have the correct module and arguments, and the playbook should start with \'---\' followed by the tasks.\n\nLet me structure each task step by step, making sure they\'re in the right order and that the conditions are accurately applied. I\'ll double-check the YAML syntax to prevent any linting errors, as the user emphasized compliance with yamllint and ansible-lint standards.\n\nFinally, I\'ll ensure that the playbook is self-contained and can be directly used in an Ansible Role without any modifications. That should cover all the user\'s requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install prerequisites\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n  loop:\n    - vault\n    - libgomp1\n    - python3-dev\n    - python3-pip\n\n- name: Include installation method specific tasks\n  include_tasks: "vault_{{ installation_method }}.yml"\n  when: installation_method is defined\n\n- name: Add Vault environment variables\n  set_fact:\n    keyvault_path: "/etc/vault.d/keyvault.json"\n\n- name: Include hardening tasks\n  include_tasks: hardening.yml\n\n- name: Start and enable vault\n  service:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type == "oss"\n\n- name: Enable vault\n  service:\n    name: vault\n    enabled: yes\n  when: vault_type != "oss"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T08:19:58.162567506Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 17646916996, 'load_duration': 73915002, 'prompt_eval_count': 382, 'prompt_eval_duration': 94786248, 'eval_count': 743, 'eval_duration': 17476907966, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--92d5a5ef-bf58-44aa-9afb-ce5e21177947-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 382, 'output_tokens': 743, 'total_tokens': 1125}
