content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me go through each task one by one to make sure I understand what\'s needed.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the very first line. That\'s straightforward. I\'ll make sure to include that.\n\nTask 1 is to gather OS information using "cat /etc/os-release". So I\'ll use the command module with the shell command. I\'ll register the output to a variable called os_release_info so it can be used in subsequent tasks.\n\nNext, Task 2 sets two variables: bootstrap_distribution and bootstrap_distribution_major_version. The user mentioned using a loop over a dictionary. I\'m thinking that the os_release_info variable will have a dictionary with keys like ID and VERSION_ID. So, I\'ll loop over these keys and assign their values to the respective variables.\n\nThen, Task 3 sets bootstrap_os_family based on the distribution. I\'ll need a dictionary that maps distributions to their families. For example, \'Ubuntu\' and \'Debian\' map to \'Debian\', while \'Fedora\', \'CentOS\', and \'RHEL\' map to \'RedHat\'. I\'ll loop over this dictionary and set the variable accordingly.\n\nI should ensure that each task uses the correct module and that the loops are properly structured. Also, I need to make sure that the playbook adheres to YAML and Ansible lint standards, so proper indentation and syntax are crucial.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure the playbook with three tasks, each with their respective modules and variables. I\'ll start with the \'---\' line, followed by the tasks as described.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: lookup bootstrap facts\n  command: cat /etc/os-release\n  register: os_release_info\n\n- name: set bootstrap facts (I)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_distribution: "{{ os_release_info.stdout|ansible.utils.convert_to_dict|dict2item|first.value.ID }}"\n    bootstrap_distribution_major_version: "{{ os_release_info.stdout|ansible.utils.convert_to_dict|dict2item|first.value.VERSION_ID|split(\'.\')[0] }}"\n\n- name: set bootstrap facts (II)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_os_family: "{{ lookup(\'ansible.utils.mapping\', {\n        \'Ubuntu\': \'Debian\',\n        \'Debian\': \'Debian\',\n        \'Fedora\': \'RedHat\',\n        \'CentOS\': \'RedHat\',\n        \'RHEL\': \'RedHat\'\n    }, key=bootstrap_distribution) }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T08:36:50.722910601Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9938762715, 'load_duration': 102825009, 'prompt_eval_count': 386, 'prompt_eval_duration': 101207123, 'eval_count': 518, 'eval_duration': 9733859835, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--159af2ba-9e47-47a6-8056-bbae6339e842-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 386, 'output_tokens': 518, 'total_tokens': 904}
