content="<think>\nAlright, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user's detailed instructions. Let me break down the tasks step by step to ensure I cover everything correctly.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with '---' on the first line, so I'll make sure to include that. It should be a valid YAML file, so proper indentation and syntax are crucial. The tasks need to be in a specific order and structure as provided.\n\nTask 1 is to install apache httpd. I'll use the apt module for Debian-based systems and yum for others, but since the user didn't specify, I'll assume the correct module is used with the appropriate package name.\n\nTask 2 involves configuring SELinux if it's enabled. I'll use the selinux module to modify sebooleans and set the custom port. I'll set a default port like 8080 as a placeholder but note that it should be replaced with the actual port.\n\nTask 3 requires configuring httpd with a template. I'll use the template module for /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf and include notify to run a test and restart the service. The notify handler should be defined elsewhere, so I'll just reference it here.\n\nTask 4 is specific to Debian to activate the httpd module. I'll use the a2enmod command and include a notify handler again.\n\nTask 5 and 6 involve importing other YAML files based on conditions. I'll use import_tasks with the necessary conditions, checking for variables like https_ssl_enable and httpd_locations.\n\nTask 7 is similar to Task 6 but for vhosts.yml. Again, I'll use import_tasks with the condition on httpd_vhosts.\n\nTask 8 configures ports for Debian or Suse using a template. I'll use the template module and notify the test handler.\n\nTask 9 imports directories.yml if httpd_directories is set, so another import_tasks call here.\n\nTask 10 flushes handlers to ensure all notifications run. I'll include the flush_handlers command.\n\nTask 11 removes the default HTML file if a condition is met. I'll use the file module with state=absent.\n\nFinally, Task 12 starts and enables the httpd service using systemctl.\n\nI'll make sure each task is correctly ordered and that all modules and parameters are as specified. I'll also ensure that variables and conditions are properly referenced without hardcoding values where variables are intended to be used.\n\nI should double-check the YAML structure for any indentation issues and ensure that all tasks are valid within an Ansible Role's tasks/main.yml file. No extra headers like hosts or vars are needed since it's part of a role.\n\nI think I've covered all the tasks as described. Now, I'll structure the playbook accordingly, making sure each task follows the correct syntax and order.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install apache httpd\n  apt:\n    name: apache2\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  selinux:\n    boolean: httpd_setsebool\n    value: on\n    persist: true\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: httpd.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0o0644\n  notify: test_httpd_config\n\n- name: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  command: a2enmod httpd\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'\n  notify: test_httpd_config\n\n- name: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n  when: https_ssl_enable | default('false')\n\n- name: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n  when: httpd_locations | default('false')\n\n- name: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n  when: httpd_vhosts | default('false')\n\n- name: Configure ports\n  template:\n    src: ports.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/apache2/ports.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0o0644\n  when: ansible_os_family in ['Debian', 'Suse']\n  notify: test_httpd_config\n\n- name: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n  when: httpd_directories | default('false')\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  flush_handlers: yes\n\n- name: Removing default html\n  file:\n    path: /var/www/html/index.html\n    state: absent\n  when: httpd_remove_example | default('false')\n\n- name: Start and enable httpd\n  service:\n    name: apache2\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  become: yes\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T09:41:37.449840315Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 18386055605, 'load_duration': 97618077, 'prompt_eval_count': 633, 'prompt_eval_duration': 363412734, 'eval_count': 1005, 'eval_duration': 17923075566, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a3243b90-9e83-41ad-ad38-2a9a55ff8651-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 633, 'output_tokens': 1005, 'total_tokens': 1638}
