content='<think>\nAlright, so I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. The user specified that the playbook must adhere strictly to certain instructions, including starting with \'---\' and being a valid YAML file. It should also be structured to fit into an Ansible Role under the tasks directory, like tasks/main.yml.\n\nFirst, I\'ll go through each task one by one and figure out the appropriate Ansible modules to use. \n\nTask 1 is to create an OpenSSL private key. I remember that the \'openssl_privatekey\' module is used for generating private keys. The key should be stored in a specific directory, say \'/etc/ssl/private\', with the filename \'ssl.key\'. I\'ll set the \'state\' to \'present\' and specify the \'path\' for the key. Also, I\'ll use \'dest\' to set the directory and mode 0600 for security.\n\nNext, Task 2 is creating a CSR from the private key. The \'openssl_csr\' module seems right here. It will generate a Certificate Signing Request. I\'ll need to provide the privatekey_path, specify \'path\' for the CSR file, and set the common name and other details as required. Again, I\'ll set the directory and mode.\n\nTask 3 involves creating a self-signed certificate from the CSR. The \'openssl_certificate\' module should handle this. I\'ll point it to the CSR path, specify the certificate\'s path, and set the validity period to 365 days.\n\nFor Task 4, exporting to a PKCS#12 file. The \'openssl_pkcs12\' module is appropriate here. It will combine the private key and certificate into a .pfx file. I\'ll provide both the key and cert paths, set the destination, and ensure the correct format.\n\nTask 5 is reading the private key. The \'file\' module can be used to read the content of the key file and store it in a variable. Similarly, Task 6 will use the \'file\' module to read the certificate file.\n\nTask 7 requires combining the private key and certificate into a single file. The \'combine\' module from the \'community.general\' collection can concatenate the two files. I\'ll set the correct paths and mode for the new file.\n\nI also need to ensure that all tasks are in the correct order. Creating the key first, then the CSR, certificate, PKCS#12, and then reading and combining. This makes sense because each subsequent task depends on the previous one.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, arguments, and set the \'become\' to true and \'remote_tmp\' directory as \'/tmp\' since it\'s a common practice for Ansible tasks.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the YAML syntax is correct, no extra comments, and the playbook starts with \'---\' followed by the tasks in order. I\'ll double-check each module\'s parameters and ensure they are correctly specified to avoid any errors during execution.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: create | Create ssl key\n  openssl_privatekey:\n    path: /etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\n    state: present\n    dest: /etc/ssl/private\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Create ssl csr\n  openssl_csr:\n    privatekey_path: /etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\n    path: /etc/ssl/csr/ssl.csr\n    common_name: example.com\n    org_name: Example Inc.\n    country_name: US\n    state: California\n    city: San Francisco\n    dest: /etc/ssl/csr\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Create ssl certificates\n  openssl_certificate:\n    path: /etc/ssl/certs/ssl.crt\n    csr_path: /etc/ssl/csr/ssl.csr\n    validity: 365\n    dest: /etc/ssl/certs\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Create PKCS#12 file\n  openssl_pkcs12:\n    name: /etc/ssl/pkcs12/ssl.pfx\n    privatekey_path: /etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\n    certificate_path: /etc/ssl/certs/ssl.crt\n    format: pkcs12\n    dest: /etc/ssl/pkcs12\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Read private key\n  file:\n    path: /etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\n    state: read\n    content: "{{ lookup(\'file\', \'/etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\') }}"\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Read certificate\n  file:\n    path: /etc/ssl/certs/ssl.crt\n    state: read\n    content: "{{ lookup(\'file\', \'/etc/ssl/certs/ssl.crt\') }}"\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n\n- name: create | Create combined private_key and certificate file\n  combine:\n    files:\n      - /etc/ssl/private/ssl.key\n      - /etc/ssl/certs/ssl.crt\n    dest: /etc/ssl/combined/ssl.pem\n    mode: 0600\n  become: true\n  remote_tmp: /tmp\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T09:48:29.967084704Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 24992876298, 'load_duration': 103883199, 'prompt_eval_count': 422, 'prompt_eval_duration': 124598051, 'eval_count': 1185, 'eval_duration': 24763259639, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--f5eb8287-0bf5-4ead-a812-e3f8d445b737-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 422, 'output_tokens': 1185, 'total_tokens': 1607}
