ld also check if any other parts of the tasks are affected, but from the errors, it seems only the module names are the issue. The parameters like \'name\', \'state\', \'update_cache\', and \'notify\' should remain unchanged.\n\nSo, the corrected playbook will have each module replaced with its FQCN as per the ansible-lint requirements.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Ensure conflicting packages are removed\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ core_dependencies_conflicting_packages }}"\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Ensure required packages are installed\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ core_dependencies_packages }}"\n    state: present\n    update_cache: true\n  notify: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  ansible.builtin.meta:\n    flush_handlers: true' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T10:15:03.694499052Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11670947634, 'load_duration': 77839429, 'prompt_eval_count': 1445, 'prompt_eval_duration': 664981212, 'eval_count': 613, 'eval_duration': 10926556199, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7ba1d295-7d97-44d5-96ee-878cbe8c317d-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1445, 'output_tokens': 613, 'total_tokens': 2058}
