rrectly formatted, with each task as a dictionary under the 'tasks' list. Proper indentation is crucial in YAML.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I'll write the playbook starting with '---', then the tasks in order. Each task will have the correct module, parameters, and any necessary notifications or meta commands.\n\nI think that's all. Let me write the YAML accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create etcd group\n  group:\n    name: etcd\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create etcd user\n  user:\n    name: etcd\n    shell: /bin/nologin\n    groups: etcd\n    state: present\n\n- name: Copy systemctl config file for kernel hardening\n  copy:\n    src: 60-rke2-cis.conf\n    dest: /etc/sysctl.d/60-rke2-cis.conf\n    mode: 0600\n  notify: systemd-sysctl restart\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: true\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T10:57:41.697208199Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15526640651, 'load_duration': 76766953, 'prompt_eval_count': 391, 'prompt_eval_duration': 108159770, 'eval_count': 720, 'eval_duration': 15340387662, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--b1828196-e5e0-45c4-9cfa-c8aa9185fdb7-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 391, 'output_tokens': 720, 'total_tokens': 1111}
