arts with '---' and that each task is correctly ordered and named as per the instructions. Also, I'll make sure to use the appropriate become privileges since some tasks require root access.\n\nI should avoid adding any hosts, vars, or playbook-level headers since the user specified that the output should only contain the tasks. The playbook must be valid within an Ansible Role, so I'll structure it as tasks in main.yml.\n\nI'll also double-check the YAML syntax to ensure it's valid, adhering to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. Each task should have the correct module, parameters, and arguments as specified.\n\nOne potential issue is ensuring that the correct OS family is targeted for each task. For example, using apt for Debian and dnf for RedHat. I might need to use conditionals, but the user didn't specify, so I'll assume that each task is run on the appropriate system type.\n\nAnother consideration is file permissions. I'll set the group to root and mode 0755 for the scripts and directories to ensure proper permissions.\n\nFinally, I'll make sure that each task is included in the correct order, from updating caches to installing packages, creating directories, setting up scripts, configuring keepalived, and enabling the service, ending with flushing handlers.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Update apt cache\n  apt:\n    state: present\n    cache_valid_time: 3600\n\n- name: Update dnf cache\n  dnf:\n    state: present\n    cache_valid_time: 3600\n\n- name: Install packages\n  apt:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Create directory for keepalived\n  file:\n    path: /etc/keepalived\n    state: directory\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for Debian OS family\n  template:\n    src: k8s_api_healthcheck.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_healthcheck.sh\n    remote_src: yes\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for RedHat OS famliy\n  template:\n    src: k8s_api_healthcheck_redhat.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_healthcheck_redhat.sh\n    remote_src: yes\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for Debian OS family\n  template:\n    src: rke2_server_healthcheck.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2_server_healthcheck.sh\n    remote_src: yes\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for RedHat OS family\n  template:\n    src: rke2_server_healthcheck_redhat.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2_server_healthcheck_redhat.sh\n    remote_src: yes\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create keepalived config file\n  template:\n    src: keepalived.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf\n    remote_src: yes\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n\n- name: Enable keepalived and make sure it is not masked\n  service:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:21:13.506231965Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 19538739723, 'load_duration': 2499872326, 'prompt_eval_count': 558, 'prompt_eval_duration': 370353286, 'eval_count': 1196, 'eval_duration': 16667941430, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--434a2d3c-f6a6-4cf6-8d62-3ddb45737bd2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 558, 'output_tokens': 1196, 'total_tokens': 1754}
