content="<think>\nOkay, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors reported.\n\nFirst, I see that there are issues with using the correct FQCN for modules like apt, dnf, file, template, service, and meta. Ansible-lint is complaining that we're not using the fully qualified names. So, I should replace 'apt' with 'ansible.builtin.apt', 'dnf' with 'ansible.builtin.dnf', 'file' with 'ansible.builtin.file', and so on.\n\nNext, there are problems with octal values. The playbook uses numbers like 0755 and 0644 directly, which YAML interprets as octal. To fix this, I need to convert these to decimal or use quotes. But since Ansible expects them as octal, I'll just change them to decimal numbers without quotes.\n\nLooking at the tasks, I need to ensure that each module call is updated to use the correct FQCN. For example, the first task uses 'apt:', so I'll change that to 'ansible.builtin.apt:'. Similarly, the 'dnf' module in the second task should be 'ansible.builtin.dnf:'.\n\nThe third task installs packages using 'apt', which should also be updated to 'ansible.builtin.apt:'. I should also check if 'become: true' is necessary, but since the original playbook included it, I'll keep it for now.\n\nThe fourth task creates a directory with 'file:', so I'll change that to 'ansible.builtin.file:'. The same applies to all other tasks using 'template:', 'service:', and 'meta:'.\n\nFor the octal values, I'll update 'mode: 0755' to 'mode: 755' and 'mode: 0644' to 'mode: 644'. This way, YAML doesn't interpret them as octal, and Ansible will treat them as decimal.\n\nI'll go through each task and make the necessary changes step by step, ensuring that I don't alter the task names or the overall structure, just fixing the module calls and octal values.\n\nAfter making all these changes, I'll test the playbook again with ansible-lint to ensure all errors are resolved.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Update apt cache\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    state: present\n    cache_valid_time: 3600\n\n- name: Update dnf cache\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    state: present\n    cache_valid_time: 3600\n\n- name: Install packages\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  become: true\n\n- name: Create directory for keepalived\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/keepalived\n    state: directory\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for Debian OS family\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: k8s_api_healthcheck.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_healthcheck.sh\n    remote_src: true\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for RedHat OS famliy\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: k8s_api_healthcheck_redhat.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_healthcheck_redhat.sh\n    remote_src: true\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for Debian OS family\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: rke2_server_healthcheck.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2_server_healthcheck.sh\n    remote_src: true\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for RedHat OS family\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: rke2_server_healthcheck_redhat.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2_server_healthcheck_redhat.sh\n    remote_src: true\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create keepalived config file\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: keepalived.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf\n    remote_src: true\n    group: root\n    mode: 644\n\n- name: Enable keepalived and make sure it is not masked\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  ansible.builtin.meta:\n    flush_handlers: true\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:22:18.183311563Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', '