 the OS. However, in the playbook, each task is separate, so I'll include all of them in order.\n\nI also need to make sure that each task uses the correct module and parameters. For example, on RedHat, using yum with the name parameter as 'ansible'. Similarly, on Ubuntu, using apt with the name 'ansible'.\n\nFor Task 1, detecting the package state might involve checking if the package is installed or not, possibly using the package module with state=present or absent. But I'm not entirely sure how to structure that. Maybe using a shell command to check if the package is installed and then conditionally installing it. Alternatively, using the package module with a state.\n\nBut perhaps the user wants to set the package state based on the installation method. So if Ansible is installed via a package manager, ensure it's up to date, and if installed via pip, handle that separately.\n\nI think each task after Task 1 is OS-specific, so I'll structure them with the appropriate become privileges since Ansible modules often require sudo access.\n\nFinally, I'll compile all these tasks into a YAML playbook, starting with '---', and make sure each task is correctly indented and uses the right modules and parameters without any comments or explanations, as per the instructions.\n\nI should double-check that the YAML is valid and adheres to the linting standards. No trailing spaces or incorrect indentation. Also, ensure that each task is properly structured as an Ansible task with the correct keys like name, module, args, etc.\n\nI think that's all. Now, I'll proceed to write the playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Set the package state based on how Ansible is installed\n  shell: dpkg -s ansible 2>/dev/null || yum -q info ansible 2>/dev/null || pip list ansible 2>/dev/null\n  register: ansible Installation\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on RedHat\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  yum:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Fedora\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  dnf:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Ubuntu\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Debian\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible using Pip\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  pip:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:42:10.459769746Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 22034534350, 'load_duration': 90618792, 'prompt_eval_count': 392, 'prompt_eval_duration': 106789248, 'eval_count': 1026, 'eval_duration': 21835777945, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--ccaff467-d565-4ef2-af8a-0ef29c2ef4fe-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 392, 'output_tokens': 1026, 'total_tokens': 1418}
