content="<think>\nAlright, I need to fix the Ansible playbook that failed ansible-lint. Let me look at the error messages to understand what's wrong.\n\nFirst, there's an issue with the 'no-changed-when' rule. The first task uses the shell module but doesn't have a 'changed_when' specified. Since this task is just checking if Ansible is installed, it shouldn't make any changes. So, I should add 'changed_when: false' to this task to prevent it from failing the 'no-changed-when' linting rule.\n\nNext, all the module calls are using their short names like 'shell', 'yum', 'dnf', 'apt', and 'pip'. Ansible-lint is complaining because we should use their fully qualified names (FQCN) instead. This means I need to update each module call to use 'ansible.builtin.<module>' or 'ansible.legacy.<module>' depending on compatibility.\n\nLooking at each task:\n\n1. The first task uses 'shell', so I'll change it to 'ansible.builtin.shell'.\n2. The second task uses 'yum', which I'll update to 'ansible.builtin.yum'.\n3. The third task uses 'dnf', so I'll switch to 'ansible.builtin.dnf'.\n4. The fourth and fifth tasks use 'apt', which I'll replace with 'ansible.builtin.apt'.\n5. The last task uses 'pip', so I'll update it to 'ansible.builtin.pip'.\n\nI'll go through each task and make these changes. Also, for the first task, I'll add 'changed_when: false' to ensure it doesn't report a change when nothing happens.\n\nI should double-check that all other parts of the tasks remain the same, as per the instructions not to alter the functional intent or task order. Once these changes are made, the playbook should pass ansible-lint without any functional changes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Set the package state based on how Ansible is installed\n  ansible.builtin.shell:\n    cmd: dpkg -s ansible 2>/dev/null || \\\n         yum -q info ansible 2>/dev/null || \\\n         pip list ansible 2>/dev/null\n  register: ansible_installation\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on RedHat\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Fedora\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Ubuntu\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Debian\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set up Ansible using Pip\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    name: ansible\n    state: present\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:42:40.635912642Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15280191741, 'load_duration': 93401883, 'prompt_eval_count': 2301, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1646818452, 'eval_count': 667, 'eval_duration': 13538785374, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--38773813-99fc-4faf-9f18-2836ff9a06e7-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2301, 'output_tokens': 667, 'total_tokens': 2968}
