content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let\'s go through each task one by one to make sure I include everything correctly.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the very first line, so I\'ll make sure that\'s the opening.\n\nTask 1 is to import assert.yml. In Ansible, the import_tasks module is used for this. So I\'ll add a task with name "Import assert.yml" and the module import_tasks, specifying the file.\n\nNext, Task 2 is to install cron. I\'ll use the apt module with name "Install cron", state=installed, and handling the restart with restart=TRUE. Also, I\'ll set updated_cache to yes to keep the cache fresh.\n\nTask 3 is configuring the shell. The shell is usually /bin/bash, so I\'ll use the file module to write the shell file. I\'ll set the owner to root and mode to 0755. Also, I\'ll create a backup in case something goes wrong.\n\nTask 4 is about configuring the path. I\'ll use the file module again to write the path file, ensuring the content is correct. I\'ll set the same owner and mode as before.\n\nTask 5 is configuring mailto. Again, the file module will be used to set the mailto file, ensuring the correct content, owner, and mode.\n\nTask 6 is to start and enable cron. I\'ll use the service module for this. The name will be cron, state=started to start it, and enabled=TRUE to make it start on boot.\n\nFinally, Task 7 is to schedule requested cron jobs. I\'ll use the cron module, specifying the name, schedule (*/5 minutes), and the command to run. It\'s important to set the user to root and the state to present to ensure the cron job is added.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are in the correct order and that each module is used appropriately. I\'ll also check that the YAML syntax is correct, without any extra spaces or missing colons. Each task should have the correct parameters as described.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll structure the playbook with these tasks in order, ensuring it\'s valid and can be included in an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install cron\n  apt:\n    name: cron\n    state: installed\n    restart: yes\n    updated_cache: yes\n\n- name: Configure shell\n  file:\n    path: /bin/sh\n    content: \'#!/bin/bash\\n\'\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n    backup: yes\n\n- name: Configure path\n  file:\n    path: /etc/path\n    content: \'PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\'\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n    backup: yes\n\n- name: Configure mailto\n  file:\n    path: /etc/mailto\n    content: \'root\'\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n    backup: yes\n\n- name: Start and enable cron\n  service:\n    name: cron\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Schedule requested cron jobs\n  cron:\n    name: scheduled_cron_job\n    minute: */5\n    command: /usr/bin/crontab -l\n    user: root\n    state: present\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:54:01.377270688Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 17313686866, 'load_duration': 90083331, 'prompt_eval_count': 359, 'prompt_eval_duration': 88980862, 'eval_count': 756, 'eval_duration': 17133359468, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--4a1441b6-7348-41a2-ab87-a3446d865a2d-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 359, 'output_tokens': 756, 'total_tokens': 1115}
