odule can be used to locate the directory, and maybe set a fact.\n\nTask 10 is to set JAVA_HOME in /etc/environment. Using the file module to append or set the variable.\n\nI also need to ensure that each task uses the correct module and parameters, and that the playbook is valid YAML without any extra lines or comments. Since the tasks are numbered, I\'ll list them in order, each as a YAML task entry.\n\nI should also check if any tasks are OS-specific. For example, using apt_repository implies Debian/Ubuntu, but Ansible can handle different systems. Maybe I should use the apt module with become privileges, but the user didn\'t specify, so I\'ll proceed with what\'s given.\n\nPutting it all together, each task will be a separate entry under the tasks key, with the appropriate module and arguments. I\'ll make sure each task is correctly indented and follows YAML syntax. No hosts or vars sections are needed since it\'s a role under tasks/main.yml.\n\nI think I have all the tasks covered, so now I\'ll structure the playbook accordingly, ensuring it starts with \'---\' and each task follows in order.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install requirements\n  apt:\n    name: bash\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install openjdk java (package)\n  apt:\n    name: openjdk\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install RPM\n  apt:\n    name: rpm\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install DEB\n  apt:\n    name: deb\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install oracle java (rpm) (repository)\n  apt_repository:\n    repo: \'deb http://download.oracle.com/otn-pki/java/8u1721/generic/pki/9bf9575402ae43679b9a545a8a7d9c5b/ /\'\n    state: present\n  apt:\n    name: java-17-oracle\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure oracle targz\n  apt:\n    name: oracle-java17-installer\n    state: present\n  file:\n    path: /etc/oracle_jdk.conf\n    content: |\n      ORACLE_JDK_VERSION=17\n      JDK_JCE_PROVIDER_ENABLED=true\n    state: present\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Install oracle java policy software (targz)\n  apt:\n    name: oracle-java17-jdk\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set alternative (targz)\n  alternatives:\n    name: java\n    path: /usr/bin/java\n    priority: 10\n\n- name: Find JAVA_HOME\n  find:\n    path: /usr/lib/jvm/java-17-oracle\n    pattern: java\n    state: directory\n  set_fact:\n    java_home: "{{ item.path | basename }}"\n\n- name: Set JAVA_HOME in /etc/environment\n  file:\n    path: /etc/environment\n    content: "JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-oracle/{{ java_home }}"\n    state: present\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-12T11:59:51.21144659Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 23117615293, 'load_duration': 77152312, 'prompt_eval_count': 465, 'prompt_eval_duration': 136464527, 'eval_count': 1101, 'eval_duration': 22902575304, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--fa8c14e3-b281-4ab2-8b64-8bfee0abc260-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 465, 'output_tokens': 1101, 'total_tokens': 1566}
